  <data key="d0">"CURRENCY TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The value of an alternative currency expressed in terms of United States dollars."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20a3929bb24620011868bc1e55295803</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVENT OF DEFAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"'Event of Default' has the meaning specified in Section 8.01."&lt;SEP&gt;"A condition defined in the Agreement that allows a Lender to set off against the Company's obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific condition that triggers a breach of agreement, allowing the lender to take remaining rights or actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Event of Default is a situation defined in loan agreements that allows the lender to demand immediate repayment of the outstanding loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Event of Default occurs when any Borrower fails to perform or observe any terms, covenants, or agreements defined in the Loan Document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd612893d5a0225fd778ba086853009a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4b020bf60daa77bdf0578ce86ca311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb93392f69f11919011ae9632eeb26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b187719dac182a293454abdbf819f856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b57613ab89c368fdc4da998c9b03876f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFICE OF FOREIGN ASSETS CONTROL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENCY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A division of the U.S. Treasury responsible for enforcing economic and trade sanctions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1677b99670ec966f5fd1919664061d01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The act under which the Company may file reports and other documents regarding financial conditions to the SEC."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1db9dc3eba353f5566836350c579edfe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLAN ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Plan Assets denote the funds of benefit plans that are governed by ERISA's compliance standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-024104f61867a710efed88937d20b566</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AVAILABILITY PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Availability Period is the timeframe during which the Borrower can draw on the loans from the Lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"the Borrowers may borrow from time to time during the Availability Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"the period from and including the Closing Date to the earliest of (a) the Maturity Date and (b) the date of termination of the Aggregate Commitments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70346a0ac74ecfe6bd503edd172112c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-213102e52aa6edea98697876f4c7a539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17156cdb19d248f88d4ee1e387dc4521</data>
</node>
