<node id="&quot;DEFAULTING LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">"'Defaulting Lender' means, subject to Section 2.13(b), any Lender that..."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Defaulting Lender is a lender that has failed to fulfill obligations as outlined in the Loan Documents, thereby affecting the lending agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Defaulting Lender is a lender that has failed to fulfill their obligations under a loan agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Defaulting Lender's Total Credit Exposure shall be disregarded in determining Required Lenders at any time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender that has failed to meet its obligations under the terms of the Loan Documents, possibly affecting the dynamics of the lending agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender who fails to meet their obligations or terms as defined in the Loan Documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lender that has failed to meet its financial obligations or requirements as stipulated in the agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lender that has failed to meet its funding obligations as specified in the loan agreement, indicating noncompliance with terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lender that has failed to meet its obligations under the terms of the loan agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any Lender that shall exercise any right of setoff against the Company or Borrower, as provided in the Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Defaulting Lender is defined as a Lender that has failed to fund its portion of the Loans and has specific consequences outlined in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Defaulting Lender refers to any Lender who is unable to fulfill their obligations, lacking the right to approve amendments or waivers under the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d8e7576d4fa2fd6cc2e422f8c5e2f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dba9e522714ac0a8717c04f114cbd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4356ca46805b368884b787be8cbc403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b4cc5b2660656388ebad9cd016c596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce242614e7c70072950823bb3955e36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1677b99670ec966f5fd1919664061d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab6e4615e53048f9d0e33ad97f0a57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a887c72da47ff4eea9f79e69a645a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b57613ab89c368fdc4da998c9b03876f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2a3e7203d34544fcfc464c159ad06f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f3e48899c511bd9c1507e3c0453d886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f074a2930435362e3f578a0827e759</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAAP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"'GAAP' means generally accepted accounting principles in the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"GAAP stands for Generally Accepted Accounting Principles that the Company and Borrowers must follow in preparing their financial statements."&lt;SEP&gt;"GAAP stands for Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, which are accounting standards used to prepare financial statements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles that the Company must adhere to when maintaining its books and records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, which guide the preparation of financial statements."</data>
