<node id="&quot;ERISA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any Borrower shall incur liability that results in a Material Adverse Effect as a result of the occurrence of any ERISA Event."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA establishes standards for the management of employee benefit plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act which influences regulations concerning pension plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, which sets standards for pension and health plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974, which sets standards for pension and health plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act, governing specific employee benefits and liabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act, which sets standards for pension and health plans in the private sector."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1db9dc3eba353f5566836350c579edfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1677b99670ec966f5fd1919664061d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4b020bf60daa77bdf0578ce86ca311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f878f9bb708e5f123411182579bddcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-024104f61867a710efed88937d20b566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14cd42fa4cdb6464f56e1335cae13d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2a3e7203d34544fcfc464c159ad06f</data>
</node>
