<node id="&quot;MATERIAL ADVERSE EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DEFINITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A standard clause in contracts that allows one party to terminate the contract if significant negative changes in the business occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Explains adverse changes impacting the financial condition or obligations of the Company or Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liabilities incurred by a Borrower or any Material Subsidiary that results in adverse conditions significantly hindering operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Material Adverse Effect refers to a significant negative impact on the Borrowers' financial condition that may result from legal non-compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a significant negative impact that could arise from non-payment of Taxes, affecting the Company's operations and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to any event or circumstance that could have a significant negative impact on the Borrower’s financial condition or operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1db9dc3eba353f5566836350c579edfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1677b99670ec966f5fd1919664061d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4b020bf60daa77bdf0578ce86ca311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b1b3dbc667d28f3ba91031c5a47a78d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f878f9bb708e5f123411182579bddcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14cd42fa4cdb6464f56e1335cae13d8</data>
